/**
 * APO judge census (wb-021.9 cut #2): test/workbench-apo-citation-status-judge-census.test.ts holds the 19 named cases below over
 * test/helpers/apo-citation-status-judge.ts (moved from wb-021.6 FINAL cut #5 cdea135d), 410 probes in all. A case claims exactly
 * its title: each probe is judged as a whole file, and its full Judgement (kinds, unit and string counts, citation positions and
 * squeezed keys, banner membership, findings), its BOUND reading, its run-guard count (one per judgeFiles call) and, where the
 * probe lists them, its causes must equal the probe's literal. A title names the forms its probes hold; any other form of the same
 * reader is NOT CLAIMED by this census, and no residual is claimed.
 * Rows: U1..U5 are the five clauses of wb-021.9's tracker-export description, one case per clause quote (the quote is ANCHOR
 * data, the title is the claim). R-B205 gives the three members that ruling folded into this bead their own cases. G24 holds the
 * gate-prep-24 refusal #1 witnesses beside further probes of the same readers.
 * MUTANTS maps each of the twelve named members (refusal #4's nine G16 members, R-B205's three GP18 members) to a case it reds;
 * a member may red other cases too. This census does not run them: the cutting seat and the gate replay each as an edited helper.
 * SHAPE freezes the rows, each case's title digest and probe ids with text digests, and the MUTANTS pairs. ANCHOR holds the rows,
 * the MUTANTS record and the plants outside records name against those records: U1..U5 against the description's clause quotes,
 * its per-clause G16 counts and its 8000; R-B205 against the fold record and G24 against the refusal #1 note's witness ids, both in
 * the same export row's notes; the twelve member names against wb-021.6's notes. COVERAGE holds the white-space, BLANK,
 * negation-word and wrapper families against the engine's \s, the helper's BLANK and NEGATION_BEFORE and the five wrapper kinds,
 * and U3's "every footnote reference" against a line of two or more references.
 * Expected readings were measured with this judge and reviewed against the gates' own readings where a gate measured one; they
 * are observations, not an independent oracle. Display paths added: none. No scratch allocated, no source/docs edited.
 */
